# Build context for ./web — used by web/Dockerfile.
#
# This file is required in addition to the one in the repo root: Docker reads
# the ignore file at the root of the *build context*, and the web service is
# built with `context: ./web`, so the root .dockerignore is never consulted.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` after `npm ci`. Without the node_modules rule
# below, the host's node_modules would be copied over the freshly installed
# one — including native binaries built for the host platform, which breaks
# the arm64 image built on an amd64 runner.
#
# Kept in the context (the build needs them): package.json, package-lock.json,
# index.html, tsconfig.json, vite.config.ts, src/, nginx.conf.

node_modules
dist
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Vite reads .env files at build time — keep local ones out of the image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
